    },
    "body": "`mining_prioritisetransaction.py` checks that `prioritisetransaction` alone makes `getblocktemplate` return a new block, by comparing the whole template before and after moving mocktime 10 seconds forward. But `curtime` comes from the clock, so the two templates always differ, even if the template wasn't rebuilt.\n\nThis PR checks that the deprioritised transaction drops out of the template instead. \nIf you remove the counter bump in `CTxMemPool::PrioritiseTransaction` (the fix this check was added for in #10196), the test from master still passes but this one fails.",
    "labels": [
