      "body": "I verified that the check on master is effectively vacuous. Removing the `prioritisetransaction` call still makes the test pass (exit 0), while the PR correctly fails with an AssertionError. A mutation removing `++nTransactionsUpdated` is also caught by the PR but passes on master.\n\nThe issue is that `curtime` gets refreshed even when the cached block template is reused, so the existing check never actually verifies the intended update. The PR also relies on the +10s mocktime bump, without which its test fails.\n\nThese results confirm that the PR makes the test meaningfully validate the transaction prioritisation behavior.\n",
