      "body": "tACK 3066c8e\r\n\r\nConfirmed that the check on master cannot fail because `curtime` is refreshed on every `getblocktemplate` call. So the `setmocktime(mock_time+10)` bump makes the two templates not the same whether or not a rebuild happened.\r\n\r\nTested this out by commenting out `++nTransactionsUpdated` in `CTxMemPool::PrioritiseTransaction` and rebuilding it. And so on master, `assert_not_equal(template, new_template)` still passes, but with this PR, `assert tx_id not in template_txids()` fails. But the PR test passes again once the line is restored.",
